invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_power returns without wiping its table, so the sixteen
  powers of the message stay in the dead frame after every signature,
  and a later caller's uninitialized stack reads them. No output changes,
  so no vector notices. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below one
  call and requires no limb of any power in the copy.

--- old
    ct_wipe(&table, sizeof table);
    ct_wipe(pick, sizeof pick);
--- new
    ct_wipe(pick, sizeof pick);
